sentences.l:
I wrote to you, O my desire, a letter * of what I meet of the pain of the parting:
And the first of its lines: fire in my heart; * and its second: my passion and my longing;
And its third: my life and my patience have perished; * and its fourth: all the ardour (is) remaining;
And its fifth: when (will) my eye see you? * and its sixth: when (is) the day of the meeting?

sentences.i:
I have written you a letter, my heart's desire, * of all I suffer from the pain of parting.
Its first line is a fire within my heart, * its second is my passion and my longing;
Its third: my life and patience are used up; * its fourth: my ardour lives on, every bit;
Its fifth: when will my eyes behold you? * Its sixth: when comes the day we meet?
